    "\n",
    "  - *Samson’s Law* (the harmonic stability control) closed the loop by implying there are self-correcting feedback loops in nature that ensure these recurrences don’t diverge – analogous to how an ecosystem self-regulates or how a thermostat keeps temperature in range. (It’s named law in the doc, but acts like a principle that systems have internal mechanisms to curb runaway behavior and enforce harmonic bounds.)\n",
